From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:03:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: promote the staged workflows and retire clib.yml

The Phase 0 bootstrap could not push .github/workflows/ (its token
lacked the workflow scope), so three edits waited in ci/workflows/.
This promotes them, as ci/README.md said to:

- ci.yml: yaml and expr join the siblings in deps; expr for the
  resolver (#2), which builds on its tree layer.
- rust.yml: the yaml clone, the openapi/ checkout, and path filters for
  this repository's files. The live copy stopped at the gate script's
  sibling check because it cloned no yaml.
- clib.yml: deleted. It built go/clib/, which went with the ZON
  grammar, so it failed on any pull request that touched go/. Admin's
  tasks/clib-template/ brings it back as libtabnasopenapi.

ci/workflows/ goes in the same change, and ci/README.md and AGENTS.md
now say nothing is staged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
